# Production migrations log

Append-only record: one row every time a migration from `{{MIGRATIONS_DIR}}` is applied
to the **production** instance, never the sandbox — the sandbox doesn't need a log, it's
where free experimentation happens.

If migrations already existed in production before this log was created, don't try to
reconstruct that history — note the baseline here instead (date, how many, how it was
confirmed to match what's in `{{MIGRATIONS_DIR}}`) and start the log with the first
migration pushed to production after that date.

## Procedure before adding a row (see the `verify-rls` skill, section 2, and `CLAUDE.md`)

1. Migration written as a file in `{{MIGRATIONS_DIR}}`, passes `node .claude/skills/verify-rls/scripts/check-migrations-schema-only.mjs` (schema-only, or an explicit, reviewed `-- ALLOW-DML: <reason>`).
2. Applied to the **sandbox** instance first.
3. Verified there — if it touches RLS/access, real per-role queries are run (`verify-rls` section 3); if it's a pure schema change, confirmed it doesn't break anything existing.
4. Explicit confirmation from {{OWNER_NAME}} that it's ready for production — never automatic, never triggered by a merge or a push.
5. Applied to production, and **at that same moment** (not after) the row below is added.

