## Log — serverless/edge function deploys

**Why this section exists.** A deploy pipeline that rebuilds the app on push usually does **not** redeploy serverless functions. So a change to one can sit merged in the repo indefinitely while production keeps running the old code, and **nothing signals the gap** — the repo looks correct and production disagrees. That happened for four days on the project this kit was hardened against, and it's what created this section.

**Compare deployed code by content hash, never by version number.** Two environments can sit at different version numbers with byte-identical code, simply because one was deployed more times. A function believed to be diverged turned out to be identical; only the hash settles it.

| date | function | env | content hash | deployed by | {{OWNER_NAME}} confirmed | notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

