## Log — one-off data scripts against production

**Why this section exists.** Migrations are schema only (`CLAUDE.md` → the migrations rule). A one-time data fix therefore lives **outside** the versioned migrations folder — which meant, until this section existed, that a mass `UPDATE` or `DELETE` against real rows left **no trace anywhere**. Schema changes were logged and data changes were not, even though data changes are the ones you cannot roll back with a re-run.

Every script that touches production rows gets a row here, at the moment it runs. Keep a reversible backup where the operation allows one, and say in `notes` where it lives.

| date | script | rows affected | backup taken | {{OWNER_NAME}} confirmed | notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
